  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      406.27,
      455.9,
      473.42
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2: This clause inserts new section 122A in the Code of Criminal Procedure Act,No. 15 of 1979 and the legal effect of the amendment is to enable the officer in charge of apolice station to cause, a child of, or above twelve years of age and under fourteen, allegedto have committed an offence, to be examined with the consent of the parent or guardian ofsuch child, by a Government medical officer or other expert in the relevant field, in order toassist the Magistrate to form his opinion on the maturity of understanding of such child, toact in compliance with the provisions of section 76 of the Penal Code.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
